    "angles": "- Audi just quit. After 32 years it stopped taking A8 orders in February 2026, with no successor confirmed -- the segment's third player walked away.\n- Through June 2026 Audi sold 513 A8s in America, down 31 percent. BMW's 7 Series leads on 5,181, still down 9 percent. The whole segment is down 16 percent, and the S-Class is the only one going up.\n- When the radar sees a side impact coming, the suspension lifts the whole car about three inches in a few tenths of a second, so the crash hits the door sill instead of your ribs.",
